 *
 * - `nav`: groups, in the order a reader reaches for them. The first group has
 *   no heading and holds the ways in; a later group takes a `heading` only when
 *   its rows share a subject the reader would name. `children` for a section
 *   whose own pages are destinations, one level deep. Who may see a row is a
 *   function of the viewer: `nav: (viewer) => [...]`, with
 *   `viewer.can('entitlement')`. No Settings row: Settings is the account
 *   menu's.
 * - `brand.wordmark`: a wordmark image (a URL) drawn in place of the title's
 *   text, which stays the home link's accessible name.
 * - `accountLinks`: extra rows in the account menu (an Admin route), after
 *   Settings. `admin: true` shows one only to a caller holding `admin`;
 *   `entitlement: 'name'` only to a caller holding that entitlement.
 * - `paletteGroups`: extra groups of destinations in the ⌘K palette, as an
 *   array or `(viewer) => [...]`. The palette already lists the nav (a child
 *   as "Section · page"), the account's commands, and an Ask row for each
 *   chat persona.
 * - Name rows in the reader's words, never the library's architecture
 *   (canonical-app-shape.md §Milton is a person, not a place).
 *
 * What a SCREEN is rides its route's load data: `pageType` (`reading` by
 * default, `panel`, `tool`), `title` (the breadcrumbs' last crumb, which also
 * names the page for a screen reader) and `breadcrumbs` for a detail deeper
 * than the rail's row. Never a layout of the route's own.
 */
